's chat to invoke it: ",[334,335,87],"a",{"href":336},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Fagents\u002Fskills",[338,339,344],"pre",{"className":340,"code":341,"language":342,"meta":343,"style":343},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","npx skills add k90325248\u002Fshuo-ui\n","bash","",[317,345,346],{"__ignoreMap":343},[347,348,351,355,359,362],"span",{"class":349,"line":350},"line",1,[347,352,354],{"class":353},"sBMFI","npx",[347,356,358],{"class":357},"sfazB"," skills",[347,360,361],{"class":357}," add",[347,363,364],{"class":357}," k90325248\u002Fshuo-ui\n",[366,367,368,380],"ul",{},[369,370,371,372,375,376,379],"li",{},"Cursor can install it with one click from the \"Install Skill\" button on the docs page, Claude Code uses ",[317,373,374],{},"claude skill add",", and other tools can reference ",[317,377,378],{},"skills\u002Fshuo-ui\u002FSKILL.md"," on GitHub directly.",[369,381,382,383,386,387,390],{},"The skill files live in ",[317,384,385],{},"skills\u002Fshuo-ui"," of the public repo and are also published at ",[317,388,389],{},"\u002F.well-known\u002Fskills\u002F"," on the docs site. The package does not include them, so what you install is the same as 1.2.0.",[309,392,394],{"id":393},"llmstxt","📄 LLMs.txt",[300,396,397,398,406,407,414,415,418,419],{},"The docs site provides ",[334,399,403],{"href":400,"rel":401},"https:\u002F\u002Fk90325248.github.io\u002Fshuo-ui\u002Fllms.txt",[402],"nofollow",[317,404,405],{},"\u002Fllms.txt"," (an index of every page) and ",[334,408,411],{"href":409,"rel":410},"https:\u002F\u002Fk90325248.github.io\u002Fshuo-ui\u002Fllms-full.txt",[402],[317,412,413],{},"\u002Fllms-full.txt"," (the full documentation), and every page has a markdown version: add ",[317,416,417],{},".md"," to its URL. Give these URLs to tools such as ChatGPT or Claude so they answer from the docs: ",[334,420,82],{"href":421},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Fagents\u002Fllms-txt",[304,423,425],{"id":424},"docs